  "aboutDescription": "Mi Ruta Trujillo is a digital application that allows users to plan public transport trips in the city of Trujillo, Peru. Through the platform, users can look up routes, identify stops, and learn about transport vehicle itineraries to reach their destination more quickly and efficiently. The tool uses information validated by transport authorities to provide reliable data that improves the urban mobility experience.\n\nThis application was developed within the framework of the Cities in Motion (CIMO) project, implemented by the Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) on behalf of the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ), with co-financing from the Swiss State Secretariat for Economic Affairs (SECO). Development was supported by the Ministry of Transport and Communications of Peru (MTC), through the National Program for Sustainable Urban Transport (PROMOVILIDAD), in coordination with the Provincial Municipality of Trujillo.",
